--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
In math, The determinant is a scalar-valued function of the entries of a square matrix. 
The determinant of a matrix A is commonly denoted det(A), det A, or |A|. 
Its value characterizes some properties of the matrix and the linear map represented, on a given basis, by the matrix. 
The determinant is nonzeor IFF the matrix is invertible and the corresponding linear map is an isomorphism. 
However, if the determinat is zero, the matrix is reffered to as singular, meaning it does not have an inverse
 
